1
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,560
What a coincidence.

2
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,600
Wu Dongsheng's team is at Wasp-Waist Valley right now.

3
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,240
Good.

4
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,040
That's a true 1st Battalion Reconnaissance Squad Leader.

5
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,560
Report any updates immediately.

6
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,120
Yes, sir!

7
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:45,640
Battalion Commander.

8
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,840
The stone bridge at Wasp-Waist Valley is broken.

9
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:48,760
Broken?

10
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,040
This is the info they just sent about the stone bridge.

11
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:51,480
Look.

12
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,200
Mount up.

13
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,160
Attention all, mount up!

14
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:03,560
Battalion Commander.

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,760
Exercise Control set obstacles on the 2nd Battalion's route.

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,520
Their convoy has stopped now too.

17
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,199
Good.

18
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,760
Look. Both sides have run into trouble.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,920
And the problems are quite similar.

20
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:18,560
Interesting.

21
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:23,320
Ling Jun, what do you think they'll choose?

22
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:24,880
Me?

23
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,240
I feel like with Guo Zijian's personality,

24
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,920
he'll probably choose to build a bridge.

25
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,640
But if Jiang Shengqiang also chooses to build a bridge,

26
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,760
the 1st Battalion will still be at a time disadvantage.

27
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,640
In this weather,

28
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,720
choosing to build a bridge is too dangerous.

29
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:43,720
Right?

30
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,920
If we want to win now,

31
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:50,560
we have to make Jiang Shengqiang choose to detour.

32
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:52,880
Turning back to clear the obstacles

33
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,560
takes about as much time as their detour.

34
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:55,520
If we do that,

35
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:57,080
we might still have a glimmer of hope.

36
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,400
I don't want a glimmer of hope.

37
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,680
I want a one hundred percent winning strategy.

38
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,800
So we won't turn back.

39
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,760
We choose to build a bridge.

40
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,040
You want to build a bridge in this weather?

41
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,560
Jiang Shengqiang is no fool.

42
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,800
How can you be sure he'll definitely detour?

43
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,600
Jiang Shengqiang played a smart move,

44
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,120
but I'll make him outsmart himself.

45
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:18,160
He tried to catch me off guard,

46
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,880
so I'll counter with a grand deception.

47
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:25,480
Hurry! Clear the obstacles quickly!

48
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,480
We don't have much time left.

49
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:29,880
Hurry!

50
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,440
Faster!

51
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,720
The Support Company reported back.

52
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,360
The 1st Battalion is clearing the obstacles.

53
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,800
It looks like Guo Zijian has given up

54
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,880
on building a bridge at Wasp-Waist Valley.

55
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,200
Choosing to build a bridge in this weather,

56
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,360
that would be truly crazy.

57
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:57,560
His 1st Battalion's only choice is to turn back

58
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:59,240
to even have a chance against us.

59
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,000
Order the Support Company

60
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,880
to go behind the first obstacle

61
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,040
and set up a second one.

62
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,280
We must delay them.

63
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,520
Order all companies to take the detour and move out.

64
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,560
Yes, sir.

65
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,320
Good.

66
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:22,840
Playing it safe to secure victory.

67
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:25,720
They're taking quite a large detour.

68
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,360
Cutting off the 1st Battalion's retreat

69
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,400
bought him some time.

70
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,120
That's the best option Jiang Shengqiang had.

71
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:36,160
But why did the 1st Battalion only send a small squad to clear it,

72
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,480
while their main force stays put?

73
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,000
Sir.

74
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:43,080
I think Guo Zijian might be up to something.

75
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,600
Isn't that the 1st Battalion's 1st Company Commander, Li Songwei?

76
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,680
He's not in the Support Company.

77
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:57,800
We'll find out if we just wait and see.

78
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:07,800
Reporting!

79
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,680
Battalion Commander, the 2nd Battalion did choose the detour.

80
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:11,280
Good.

81
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,800
The road ahead is relatively open.

82
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,640
Tell the Support Company to build the bridge immediately.

83
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:16,040
Yes, sir!

84
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:09,760
Staff Officer Liang.

85
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,200
Are they going to build a bridge?

86
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,280
What is Guo Zijian trying to do?

87
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,120
They are actually building a bridge.

88
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:22,680
That's right.

89
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:25,240
When setting up the exercise plan,

90
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,360
I had the weather, the route,

91
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,320
and all the scenarios they might encounter

92
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,760
in all of their backup plans

93
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,000
carefully analyzed.

94
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,680
Including the feasibility of building a bridge at Wasp-Waist Valley in the rain.

95
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:36,360
All the data shows

96
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,440
a bridge at Wasp-Waist Valley is achievable.

97
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,520
So you're saying,

98
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,520
them clearing obstacles earlier was just a smokescreen?

99
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,000
They sure are playing mind games.

100
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,560
That's called strategy, not mind games.

101
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,880
Only those who seize every opportunity

102
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,720
can emerge as the ultimate victors.

103
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,560
Building a bridge in this environment

104
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,160
is definitely too risky.

105
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,080
Staff Officer Liu!

106
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:01,720
Yes, sir!

107
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:04,680
Notify Guo Zijian to stop building the bridge immediately.

108
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:05,480
Yes, sir.

109
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,000
Battalion Commander, the command center is calling.

110
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,400
Command center, go ahead.

111
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,240
01 orders you

112
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:17,400
to stop bridge construction immediately! Stop immediately!

113
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,320
Stop building the bridge? Why?

114
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:20,160
I repeat.

115
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,040
01 orders! 01 orders you

116
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,120
to stop bridge construction immediately! Stop immediately!

117
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,800
Reporting to the command center,

118
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,880
once an exercise directive is issued,

119
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,600
it is treated as a combat order.

120
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:34,720
It cannot be paused.

121
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,480
The exercise plan is very clear.

122
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,960
The commander of the 1st Battalion is me, Guo Zijian.

123
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,320
No one but Exercise Control has the right to interfere!

124
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:42,480
In short,

125
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,080
your 01 has overstepped his authority.

126
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:44,800
Guo!

127
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,560
If something really happens to the 1st Battalion,

128
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,840
can Guo Zijian bear the responsibility?

129
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,200
Lao Sang, let's get out and take a look.

130
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,160
Sun Xingwang!

131
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,120
Yes, sir!

132
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,280
Battalion Commander! The Support Company is all in position.

133
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,000
The 1st Battalion Reconnaissance Squad is across the valley.

134
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,000
What's the situation in the valley?

135
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,440
The detection team is choosing a suitable location.

136
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,560
But the rain is too heavy.

137
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:15,200
It might affect our overall progress.

138
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,080
I'll go take a look.

139
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,600
Will it be too dangerous?

140
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:23,960
Reporting,

141
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,000
Sir, you may not know this,

142
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,520
but in all these years of exercises,

143
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
bridge-building tasks are rarely assigned.

144
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,159
Even if they are,

145
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:39,480
they are carried out by our brigade's Support Battalion.

146
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:43,039
The support forces of each battalion

147
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,800
have basically never independently completed

148
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:46,600
tasks in such a complex environment.

149
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,120
Besides, with such heavy rain, if something goes...

150
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,960
I'm just a spectator today.

151
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,760
I won't make comments.

152
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,120
I won't take a stance.

153
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,160
You organize this however

154
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,280
you see fit.

155
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:00,920
Yes, sir.

156
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,040
Careful!

157
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,480
Battalion Commander!

158
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,080
Political Instructor!

159
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,440
Save them!

160
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,280
Battalion Commander!

161
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,000
Just what I was afraid of.

162
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,280
I really called it, didn't I?

163
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,440
Lao Suo, calm down.

164
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:35,320
Did you see that?

165
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,560
When that kid gets back,

166
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,840
I'm definitely going to teach him a lesson.

167
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,520
We'll talk about it after it's over.

168
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,400
I'll teach him a lesson!

169
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,760
Hold on tight!

170
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,640
Battalion Commander!

171
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:57,840
Careful, Battalion Commander!

172
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,320
You scared me to death, Staff Officer Liang.

173
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,040
Reporting, Battalion Commander.

174
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,200
The 1st Battalion didn't turn back.

175
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,600
They're building a bridge at Wasp-Waist Valley.

176
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:32,240
What?

177
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,240
We've been tricked.

178
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:38,160
Battalion Commander, changing routes now might be too late.

179
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,400
With weather like this,

180
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,760
the 1st Battalion might not successfully build a bridge.

181
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,760
Guo Zijian, you madman!

182
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:46,720
We can't risk it.

183
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,320
Order the troops to advance at full speed!

184
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:50,520
Yes, sir!

185
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,400
All units, all units.

186
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:55,040
Advance at full speed! Advance at full speed!

187
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:12,080
Sun Xingwang!

188
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:12,680
Sir!

189
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:17,200
I'm asking you, is the bridge secure?

190
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:17,960
Rest assured, Political Instructor.

191
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,480
The men are laying down anti-slip mats.

192
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,400
The convoy can cross shortly.

193
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:23,400
You must ensure nothing goes wrong.

194
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,640
I guarantee the mission will be accomplished!

195
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,920
Battalion Commander, I suggest personnel and equipment cross separately in order.

196
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,720
That's what I was thinking too.

197
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:36,440
Staff Officer Hu.

198
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,080
Sir!

199
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,040
Notify all units crossing the bridge.

200
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,080
Personnel and equipment are to cross separately.

201
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:40,720
Yes, sir!

202
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,800
They actually managed to build the bridge.

203
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,720
But this Guo Zijian is really quite something.

204
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,320
With one mention of overstepping authority, Deputy Brigade Commander Suo

205
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,400
was left completely speechless.

206
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,160
He wasn't wrong.

207
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,120
Once the exercise begins,

208
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,560
if the actual leaders

209
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:01,600
continue to issue commands,

210
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,560
wouldn't that ruin the simulation?

211
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:07,160
But looking at it this way,

212
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,680
isn't the 1st Battalion going to turn the tables?

213
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,520
The 1st Battalion's path forward

214
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,160
is truly full of twists and turns.

215
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:33,200
I'm going to deal with Sun Xingwang.

216
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:36,320
He's the one who guaranteed me nothing would go wrong.

217
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:37,680
Calm down.

218
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:39,680
The Reconnaissance Squad has already gone to check.

219
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,960
Staff Officer Liu.

220
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,160
Here!

221
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,440
Inform Guo Zijian

222
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,520
to see if we should

223
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,040
halt the bridge crossing and organize a rescue.

224
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:49,760
Yes, sir!

225
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:03,440
Reporting, Battalion Commander.

226
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:06,040
I'm at the cave-in site right now.

227
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:06,800
What's the situation?

228
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:09,080
Some of the dirt has come loose.

229
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:10,400
Is it a serious problem?

230
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,920
After the equipment pushed away the loose rocks,

231
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,360
the original bridge foundation was exposed.

232
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,840
I think

233
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:21,760
it can fully support the vehicles passing through.

234
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:22,840
Are you sure?

235
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,680
Give me one more minute.

236
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:42,480
Battalion Commander, the vehicles are clear to pass.

237
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:43,200
Good.

238
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,120
Staff Officer Hu!

239
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:46,760
Here, sir!

240
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,720
What's the 2nd Battalion's position?

241
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:49,880
Battalion Commander,

242
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,760
they're moving much faster

243
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,480
than we anticipated.

244
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:54,040
At their current pace,

245
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:56,600
they should reach the assembly point by 6:00 AM.

246
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,280
Looks like I still underestimated him.

247
00:14:58,960 --> 00:14:59,360
Battalion Commander,

248
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:00,800
the weather is severe.

249
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,080
Building and crossing the bridge

250
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,760
is taking longer than we expected.

251
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,520
Don't try to comfort me.

252
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,120
Until the very last moment,

253
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:08,600
it's not certain who will win.

254
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,920
Tell everyone to stay safe and cross quickly.

255
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:12,600
Yes, sir!

256
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,800
I'm sorry you had to see that, sir.

257
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:49,680
This drill felt more like real combat than an exercise.

258
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,120
Do you think Guo Zijian

259
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:53,320
was acting out of desperation,

260
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,840
or is he just completely reckless?

261
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,160
If you ask me,

262
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:57,720
he just got lucky.

263
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:59,160
Like a blind squirrel finding a nut.

264
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:00,680
My god.

265
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:01,840
It had me sweating bullets.

266
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,600
Sometimes, luck favors the prepared.

267
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:07,640
I'd actually suggest

268
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,040
you take some time to review the drill.

269
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:12,000
Watch it again from start to finish.

270
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:15,160
You might get a truer sense of it then.

271
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:16,080
Yes, sir.

272
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:16,440
Yes, sir.

273
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,440
Brothers of the 1st Battalion!

274
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,280
Let's sing a song.

275
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:04,040
"Unity." Ready, sing!

276
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:07,440
Unity is strength!

277
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:10,760
Unity is strength!

278
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:13,880
This strength is iron, this strength is steel!

279
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:17,200
Harder than iron, stronger than steel!

280
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:20,560
Fire at the fascists!

281
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,880
Let all undemocratic systems die!

282
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:38,200
Kill!

283
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,560
Guo Zijian.

284
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,240
It's not time to celebrate yet.

285
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:47,080
Yes.

286
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,400
You got here first.

287
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,040
But the entire mobilization process

288
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:53,640
will be scored.

289
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,680
You took the wrong route.

290
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,280
That's the biggest point deduction.

291
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:05,520
What adds or deducts points,

292
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,080
you don't get to decide.

293
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,560
That's up to Exercise Control.

294
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,280
All companies!

295
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,360
Fall in and head back!

296
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:19,840
Yes, sir!

297
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,920
Attention! Left wheel!

298
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:23,880
Quick time,

299
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:25,120
march!

300
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:37,360
Section Chief Liu

301
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:37,920
Yes, sir!

302
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,240
You've been keeping watch all night.

303
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,040
Are there any new developments?

304
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:43,560
Reporting, Sir!

305
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,200
Although the final results aren't out yet,

306
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,240
based on the various data

307
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:49,560
and intelligence reports,

308
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,080
the 1st Battalion reached the assembly point first.

309
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:55,040
The 1st Battalion should be the winner.

310
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:58,760
Remembering the lesson

311
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,520
is far from enough.

312
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,320
You must improve

313
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:08,680
your overall skills.

314
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,120
Scouts

315
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,920
are the eyes and ears for combat decisions.

316
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:17,960
Your accuracy

317
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:23,360
will keep your commanders' senses sharp.

318
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:25,560
Your mistakes

319
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,520
will leave your commanders

320
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:30,000
deaf and blind.

321
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:33,040
Especially under severe weather conditions.

322
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,240
Our Battalion Commander Guo

323
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,360
risked his life

324
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,240
to rescue our comrades.

325
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,560
If anything had happened to him,

326
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:42,240
Wu Dongsheng!

327
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:43,040
Here!

328
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:46,400
I believe you'd regret it for the rest of your life.

329
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:47,360
Political Instructor,

330
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:49,520
I understand.

331
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,200
I'll do a proper self-criticism.

332
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:53,960
A similar mistake

333
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,400
must never happen again.

334
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,600
I guarantee it.

335
00:19:58,680 --> 00:19:59,960
If I make another mistake,

336
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:02,320
I'll pay with my head.

337
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:09,800
Wu Dongsheng,

338
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:11,760
from start to finish,

339
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:14,480
our Battalion Commander Guo kept insisting

340
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,800
on trusting the men he uses.

341
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,400
What does this mean?

342
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:23,040
It means he highly approves of you.

343
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,440
Your head

344
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:30,520
belongs to the motherland and the people.

345
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,480
Don't go throwing it away so easily.

346
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,600
What I need is accurate intelligence.

347
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:37,680
Yes, sir.

348
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:41,440
Reporting!

349
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:42,920
This result...

350
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,720
I cannot accept it.

351
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,280
State your reasons.

352
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:48,640
For taking the wrong route,

353
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,600
why weren't points deducted?

354
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:54,240
Alright.

355
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:56,720
Since there are objections to the result,

356
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:59,160
we will now ask Exercise Control staff officer,

357
00:20:59,160 --> 00:20:59,960
Comrade Liang Hong,

358
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:01,320
to give a brief explanation.

359
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:03,360
Yes, sir.

360
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:12,840
Sirs,

361
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:16,440
this mobilization is a comprehensive assessment

362
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,400
of the combined battalion's armed march.

363
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,080
But in the process,

364
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:20,920
we also set up a few small tasks.

365
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:23,760
First, regarding the 1st Battalion's target point,

366
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:27,160
we set up two points: one dummy and one real.

367
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:29,000
They are very close to each other and hard to tell apart.

368
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:31,640
But the 2nd Battalion didn't face the same situation.

369
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:33,440
Second, for the 2nd Battalion.

370
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:36,560
Although they didn't have target point interference,

371
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:39,240
we specifically set up roadblocks on their way.

372
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,000
There was a simple mountain road 300 meters off the roadblock.

373
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:43,840
According to the preset plan,

374
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,480
after the convoy passed the simple mountain road,

375
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:48,040
they could reach the assembly area directly by building a bridge.

376
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:50,880
But the 2nd Battalion chose a long-distance detour.

377
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:55,360
After discovering the convoy's directional error,

378
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:57,800
the 1st Battalion promptly found a way out of a desperate situation.

379
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,200
This naturally gets extra points.

380
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:01,440
This was also a bonus point item

381
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:03,200
that was noted when setting up the task.

382
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:06,040
So through various comprehensive comparisons,

383
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:07,680
and judging by the time

384
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:10,320
the main combat forces of both sides arrived at the assembly area,

385
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:13,520
we concluded that the 1st Battalion won.

386
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:14,560
That is all.

387
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,520
It seems Staff Officer Liang knows

388
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:21,040
all the rules and grading standards

389
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,280
of this mobilization by heart.

390
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:25,200
Staff Officer Liang's brain

391
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:27,520
is like a small data processing center.

392
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,160
Let me add a few words.

393
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:30,520
Actually,

394
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:32,920
when Sir set up the tasks

395
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,480
for the two battalions,

396
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:36,680
he fully considered the weather factor.

397
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:40,800
So the rain last night was also one of the variables.

398
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:44,000
Namely, a convoy marching on mountain roads on a rainy night.

399
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:45,920
What commanders have to face,

400
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,480
besides military command,

401
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:49,920
is the handling of safety issues

402
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:52,240
and the courage to make prompt decisions.

403
00:22:57,080 --> 00:23:01,760
A normal rainy night combat readiness mobilization

404
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:07,200
allowed us to learn a lot from Sir

405
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:12,640
about the concepts and skills we should master in actual combat.

406
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:14,640
We also learned

407
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:17,280
what kind of comprehensive qualities

408
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:19,800
a commander needs to deal with

409
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:22,360
complex environments.

410
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:27,320
This should be the original intention

411
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,840
and true purpose of this training.

412
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,600
So next,

413
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,360
please announce the results, Sir.

414
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,200
I said earlier

415
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:37,640
that I'm just a spectator today, not a referee.

416
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:39,640
You guys discuss it yourselves.

417
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:45,240
Then Deputy Brigade Commander Suo and I

418
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:45,880
will have a quick meeting to discuss it,

419
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:47,200
and announce the results later.

420
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:47,880
All right.

421
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,560
1st Battalion, 2nd Battalion,

422
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:53,000
go back and assemble your troops first.

423
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:54,320
Yes, Sir.

424
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:21,280
Jiang Shengqiang.

425
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:23,600
Are you really that petty?

426
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:30,560
Guo Zijian.

427
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:33,240
I don't care about the outcome

428
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,320
of the main attack challenge.

429
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:37,160
A one-on-one duel.

430
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:39,040
Do you dare?

431
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:40,240
Battalion Commander Jiang,

432
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:42,680
commanders are judged by their overall skills.

433
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,280
We shouldn't let our emotions take over,

434
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:44,960
right?

435
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:46,800
Even though the 2nd Battalion and our 1st Battalion

436
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:48,200
have always been rivals,

437
00:24:48,760 --> 00:24:51,000
we are all the people's soldiers.

438
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:53,000
Unity is strength.

439
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:54,640
A weak soldier only affects himself,

440
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:56,720
but a weak commander ruins the whole unit.

441
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:01,120
Does a commander really lack this much courage?

442
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:03,040
Or is it

443
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:04,840
that you, Guo Zijian, are so used to

444
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:07,080
those dirty, underhanded tactics

445
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:08,600
that you've long forgotten

446
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,560
what true military competence is?

447
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:23,200
What do you want to compete in?

448
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:25,440
A comprehensive combat drill.

449
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:26,840
You up for it?

450
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:29,240
No problem.

451
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,520
I'll take you on.

452
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:36,160
I'm going to report to Sir right now.

453
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:43,200
Guo Zijian.

454
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,000
I know you're tough,

455
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:49,920
but Jiang Shengqiang and those boys from 1st Company...

456
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:50,880
he's different.

457
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:51,680
He's the

458
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:53,560
entire group army's

459
00:25:53,640 --> 00:25:55,960
record holder for the comprehensive combat drill.

460
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,880
You can't just agree like that.

461
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:58,040
What's wrong, Political Instructor?

462
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:58,960
You don't trust me?

463
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:01,200
Well, even the best can slip up.

464
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:03,560
I'm just worried that if you actually lose,

465
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:04,800
wouldn't that be humiliating for you?

466
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:05,800
There is no "if."

467
00:26:06,120 --> 00:26:08,000
I'll bring home the victory for you to see.

468
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:08,640
Alright?

469
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:10,080
Battalion Commander Guo.

470
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:11,040
So confident.

471
00:26:11,360 --> 00:26:12,440
We'll go cheer you on, then.

472
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,120
Are we welcome?

473
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:14,120
Of course.

474
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:16,680
I'll be even more motivated if you come.

475
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:17,560
Guo Zijian.

476
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:19,520
You've definitely let victory get to your head.

477
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:21,120
You need to keep a low profile.

478
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:21,920
Better safe than sorry.

479
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:23,320
Alright, stop it.

480
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:23,720
Better safe...

481
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:25,560
People are watching. Save me some face, will you?

482
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:28,760
Staff Officer Liang.

483
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,680
This Guo Zijian is really quite interesting.

484
00:26:32,280 --> 00:26:34,320
I feel like you two really click.

485
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:36,240
Me and him? Click?

486
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:39,760
Like last time with that Battalion Combat Group.

487
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:41,000
Even Jiang Shengqiang didn't know about it,

488
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:42,520
but you figured it out immediately.

489
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:44,160
And this time with the bridge.

490
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,680
You left room for both sides to succeed,

491
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:47,200
but only Guo Zijian actually did it.

492
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,720
I guess it's just how you geniuses think.

493
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:51,160
I wouldn't understand.

494
00:26:51,160 --> 00:26:51,440
Staff Officer Liang.

495
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:55,320
Section Chief Liu

496
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:57,160
Staff Officer Liang

497
00:26:57,480 --> 00:26:58,200
Is it convenient

498
00:26:58,480 --> 00:26:59,600
to have a private word?

499
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:00,880
Staff Officer Liang.

500
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:01,920
I'll be going now.

501
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:05,280
Staff Officer Liang.

502
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:06,440
There's a matter

503
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:07,800
regarding our brigade's

504
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:08,600
participation in this

505
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:10,920
army group exercise's overall layout and planning.

506
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:12,840
I'd like to ask for your help.

507
00:27:13,280 --> 00:27:14,480
The army group's campaign exercise

508
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:16,080
is our base's job anyway.

509
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:17,320
You're being too polite, Section Chief Liu.

510
00:27:17,840 --> 00:27:19,800
I'm sure you know the cause

511
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:20,960
of this challenge match.

512
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:23,040
But right now, the 1st and 2nd Battalions,

513
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:25,320
in order to fight for the main assault battalion position,

514
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,000
you could say

515
00:27:27,440 --> 00:27:28,200
they've clashed until

516
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:29,600
both sides are bruised,

517
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,600
affecting our unity.

518
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:31,560
And it even

519
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:32,600
makes our brigade leaders

520
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:33,600
lose face in front of

521
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:35,120
our superiors.

522
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:37,760
Has it?

523
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:41,760
Although Battalion Commander Jiang questioned the match,

524
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:43,560
I have already explained all the data

525
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:45,920
and the established rules to him.

526
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,200
The match is fair.

527
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,440
How could it affect unity?

528
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:50,160
Anyway, if this matter

529
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:52,240
isn't handled well,

530
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:53,440
not only will it

531
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:55,920
affect the troops' overall morale,

532
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:58,480
it will also affect our pre-planned

533
00:27:58,480 --> 00:27:59,560
exercise plan.

534
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:01,800
Shouldn't the exercise plan be

535
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:04,360
formulated according to the actual combat situation?

536
00:28:04,360 --> 00:28:05,640
How can it be set up in advance?

537
00:28:05,640 --> 00:28:06,600
That's unscientific.

538
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,200
You're right about that.

539
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:10,280
But there is some foundational work,

540
00:28:10,360 --> 00:28:12,040
such as setting up combat units

541
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,280
and establishing the main assault battalion.

542
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,480
We still need to prepare for these in advance.

543
00:28:16,920 --> 00:28:17,720
So then,

544
00:28:17,800 --> 00:28:19,480
is there anything I can help you with?

545
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:21,680
I was thinking,

546
00:28:22,080 --> 00:28:22,920
look,

547
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:24,960
could you reconsider

548
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:26,080
the determination of the match results?

549
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,240
Data and theoretical analysis cannot be faked.

550
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,080
I'm sorry.

551
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:40,080
Staff Officer Liang, Staff Officer Liang, don't misunderstand.

552
00:28:40,080 --> 00:28:41,320
I'm not asking you to fake it.

553
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:46,880
I just feel that Guo Zijian

554
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:48,360
is an unstable factor.

555
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:50,920
I believe

556
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,600
we both know this well.

557
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:53,960
Have you forgotten the last time

558
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:56,000
he fabricated orders?

559
00:28:56,880 --> 00:28:58,280
We were all victims of that,

560
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,000
right?

561
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:02,280
Our opponent this time is the 404th Brigade.

562
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:05,160
If we don't have a reliable main assault battalion,

563
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,480
it is very likely

564
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:08,400
to affect the final results of the match.

565
